AWS authentication system login types.
1 Aws console login.
  a . Root user : email + captcha + password
  b . IAM user
  c . Activate MFA (Multiple factor authentication )

2 Aws cli (command line interface ) login.
   a . Access keys (Access key id + secret access key)

3 Aws sdk ( Software development kit ) login.
   a . Python ,Java , login programming language.

4 Aws i am identity (aws sso ) login.
   a .Centralized center for multiple AWS accounts
   b . External identity provider.

5 Federated access login . (Corporate)

6 Temporary credentials (AWS STS).(security token service)

7 Service-Based Access


Networking for DevOps.

Network : Network is an infrastructure of two or more devices connected together for
data and resources sharing. like (router, switches, modem, NIC , (NETWORK INTERFACE CARD), chip, buses , cables)

Networking: Networking is the process of designing ,implementing and managing communication between those connected devices.

Protocol: A Protocol is a set of rules that defines how data is formatted , transmitted and received between devices/server.


It follows format in order: 1.Syntax 2.Semantics 3.Timing.

Protocol categories:
1. Communication Protocols:
It defines how data travels. TCP, UDP, ARP, FTP, SMTP

2.Network Protocols:
It defines encryption and authentication :TLS, SSL , SSH , IPsec

3.Management Protocols:
It defines network config and monitoring : DHCP ,DNS ,NTP ,SNMP

Full Form:
HTTPS = Hyper Text Transfer Protocol Secure
TCP = Transmission Control Protocol
UDP = User Datagram Protocol
ARP = Address Resolution Protocol
FTP = File Transfer Protocol
SMTP = Simple Mail Transfer Protocol

TLS = Transport Layer Security
SSL = Secure Sockets Layer
SSH = Secure Shell or (Secure Socket Shell)
IPsec = Internet Protocol Security

DHCP = Dynamic Host Configuration Protocol
DNS = Domain Name System
NTP = Network Time Protocol
SNMP = Simple Network Management Protocol

